{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 69, :comments ["<b>And He built, exalted</b> — [there is] an adjective whose noun is absent, like וּמַאֲכָלוֹ בְרִיאָה שָׂה (\"and its fare is a fat sheep/lamb\"), or עֶגְלָה (\"a fat calf\"). And so here: וַיִּבֶן בְּאַרְמְנוֹתָיו רָמִים (\"and He built in His palaces exalted ones\")." "<b>And the sense of \"like the earth\"</b> — because the earth in its totality, along with its parts, is among that which endures, therefore He mentioned this particular part of the earth that endures, corresponding to the earth in its entirety."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites the phrase to illustrate that רמים is an adjective whose head noun is elliptical; the two examples (שה, עגלה) show the missing noun could be various things — I have rendered his examples verbatim without expanding the grammatical argument."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:26.821644675Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}